      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nTucked away in a quiet cul-de-sac just off Kill Avenue, this superb three-bedroom end of terrace home combines modern comfort, generous gardens, and an exceptionally convenient location close to Monkstown and Dun Laoghaire Town Centre.\n\nBeautifully presented and comprehensively upgraded, No. 62 offers bright, well-proportioned accommodation comprising three bedrooms, a family bathroom, a welcoming living room, and a modern fitted kitchen. The property underwent an extensive programme of improvements in 2023, including a full replumb, a complete house re-wire, a new kitchen, and a new bathroom. An Ideal Vogue Max 40kW combi boiler was also installed, complemented by dual-zone heating controls and new radiators throughout the home.\n\nFurther upgrades include A-rated windows installed in 2026, an A-rated Palladio front door installed in 2025, upgraded attic insulation, and new flooring throughout with thermal underlay. The lighting and internal doors have also been upgraded, while a new ESB smart meter and smoke, heat, and carbon monoxide alarms bring the property firmly in line with modern standards. Together, these improvements create a comfortable, energy-conscious, and easy-to-maintain home that is ready for immediate occupation.\n\nOutside, the property boasts superb gardens to both the front and rear. The long rear garden enjoys excellent privacy and offers ample scope to extend the property, subject to planning permission. It also benefits from a side passageway for convenient rear access. The outdoor space is ideal for children to play, entertaining guests, or relaxed alfresco dining during the warmer months.\n\nThe location is equally impressive. Local shops at Deansgrange, Dun Laoghaire seafront, the town centre, DART services, and numerous bus routes along Kill Avenue are all within easy reach. The property is surrounded by a wide selection of excellent primary and secondary schools, with the Dun Laoghaire Institute of Art, Design and Technology directly opposite. This is an exceptionally convenient and sought-after setting for families and professionals alike.\n\nSpecial Features\n• Superb three-bedroom end of terrace home\n• Quiet cul-de-sac position just off Kill Avenue\n• On-street parking\n• Bright and spacious living accommodation\n• Modern fitted kitchen installed in 2023\n• New bathroom installed in 2023\n• Ideal Vogue Max 40kW combi boiler installed in 2023\n• Dual-zone heating controls\n• New radiators installed throughout the home\n• Full replumb completed in 2023\n• Full house rewire completed in 2023, bringing the property to modern standards\n• A-rated windows installed in 2026\n• A-rated Palladio front door installed in 2025\n• New flooring throughout with thermal underlay\n• Fully upgraded lighting\n• Upgraded attic insulation\n• Upgraded internal doors\n• New ESB smart meter installed\n• Smoke, heat, and carbon monoxide alarms installed\n• Fully upgraded and beautifully presented throughout\n• Long, private rear garden offering scope to extend, subject to planning permission\n• Well-maintained front and rear gardens\n• Side passage providing convenient rear access\n• Excellent public transport links, including DART and bus services\n• Within walking distance of Dun Laoghaire town centre and seafront\n• Close to excellent primary and secondary schools, with IADT directly opposite"
      },
